  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nUpper pattern continues to be quiet, and looks to remain quiet \nthrough Sunday, as models show a very weak and broad scale flow \nover the west, punctuated by a shallow trough over southern NV, \nand the lower Colorado river valley, and by weak riding over \nnorthern NV and ID. This flow setup looks to keep Nevada dry for \nthe next several days, however with the westerly Jet just to the \nnorth, models continue to show the pressure gradient over northern\nNevada tightening over recent runs. This will keep elevated fire \nweather conditions as westerly winds of 10 MPH to 20 MPH with \ngusts up to 35 MPH will possible over northern Humboldt and Elko \ncounties through Saturday. Elsewhere winds will be lighter out of \nthe W-SW at 5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH possible. Sunday \nthe stronger winds shift into central Nevada as a pacific trough \napproaches, shifting elevated fire weather concerns into White \nPine county. Monday, models show that northern stream upper level \ntrough moving through Nevada, The GFS and ECMWF continue to trend \nstronger and deeper with the trough with this system, while \ncontinuing to depict a fast moving system with not much moisture. \nAnother point of continuity is for light isolated showers \naccompanying trough passage Monday afternoon and evening, with the\ntrough exiting east Monday night. Tuesday and Wednesday ridging \nreturns bringing another period of quiet weather conditions back \nto the Silver State. Temperature wise a quick warming trend will \nlast through Friday as highs peak in the mid to upper 80s. \nSaturday through Tuesday a cooling trend will see temperatures \nfalling into the mid 70s for highs. Wednesday will see another \nwarming trend to finish out the week with highs returning to the \nmid 80s. Lows will range in the mid to upper 40s for the first \nhalf of the forecast period, cooling into the mid to upper 30s by \nmiddle of next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \n\nThere is high confidence in a much drier pattern lasting through \nSunday of next week.\n\nThere is low confidence in the potential for a 10% to 30% chance \nfor isolated showers across Nevada as an upper trough passes \nthrough Monday of next week.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in the return of upper level\nridging for the middle of next week restoring quiet and dry \npattern over Nevada.",
